"""
Dialogue/center gain slider for the PipeWire 7.1/5.1 -> stereo
downmix filter-chain.

Drag the slider and it live-updates "Gain 2" on both the mix_l and
mix_r builtin mixer nodes inside the filter-chain graph, using
pw-cli.  No restart of PipeWire or the filter-chain is needed.

Requirements:
    - pipewire / pw-cli installed and on PATH
    - python3-tk (Tkinter)      e.g. sudo apt install python3-tk
    - pystray + Pillow (optional, for the tray icon):
          pip install pystray pillow --break-system-packages
      If missing, the tray icon is silently skipped and the window still works.
    - your filter-chain's capture node.name (see --node-name below)

Window behavior:
    - The window sets the X11 "dialog" window-type hint, which sway/i3 use to
      auto-float windows by default - no sway.config changes needed. If you
      ever want an explicit rule (or auto-floating doesn't kick in), add:
          for_window [class="DialogueSlider"] floating enable
      to your sway config.
    - With the tray icon enabled (default), closing the window just hides it;
      use the tray menu (or its Quit item) to bring it back or exit fully.

Usage:
    python3 dialogue_slider.py
    python3 dialogue_slider.py --node-name center_adjustable_downmix_7_1
    python3 dialogue_slider.py --no-tray
"""

